@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM67kRCC -->
Verified actionable: although the original location is outdated, the helper moved to `.agents/scripts/canonical_git_worktree.py`. Fixed in 25131f77ed (pushed with merge head 9628359132): `_worktree_cwd` applies successive `-C` options before resolving relative removal targets, preserving absolute targets. Regression cases cover single/chained `-C`, absolute targets, and no `-C` in `.agents/scripts/tests/test-canonical-git-command-guard.sh:479-482`.

Verification: all 227 guard assertions pass with inherited `GIT_CONFIG_*` overrides removed from the test process; native ShellCheck and Python compilation pass.

@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM67ks_v -->
Verified actionable and addressed in 25131f77ed, integrated with concurrent fix 4122900122 in pushed head 9628359132. Both dispatch branches now run inside the RuntimeError handler in `.agents/scripts/canonical_git_policy.py:210-222`, so probe failures return controlled denials rather than escaping with a traceback.

The regression in `.agents/scripts/tests/test-canonical-git-command-guard.sh:514-535` injects failures into both dispatch branches and checks the denial result. All 227 guard assertions pass with inherited `GIT_CONFIG_*` overrides removed from the test process; Python compilation and native ShellCheck pass.

@coderabbitai Confirmed and fixed in a9342a07ec. `dispatch_metrics` now collects spawns through the same `until + 21600` look-ahead as `runtime_exits`. `spawn_count` still counts only in-window spawns, and the `start < until` guards in `pair_workers` and `open_intervals` still drop spawns at or after `until`.

Checked with your scenario (10:00–11:00 window, unpaired 10:00 spawn, 11:05 retry spawn, 11:10 exit). The exit now pairs with the 11:05 spawn, `slot_occupancy_paired_only.mean` is `None`, and the 10:00 spawn stays open.

The same bug was in the real logs. For 17:45–20:30Z, the 21:00:00 exit of `worker:issue-34781:45100:1795552431` (spawned 20:34:08) had been paired with the pre-reboot 17:05:51 spawn of the same issue. That added one false worker to the whole window: occupancy was 10.515 and is now 9.515.

@coderabbitai Verified addressed by pushed commit 90e508e994, retained at current head 89ee194ad4. `.agents/scripts/pulse-merge-process-worker-briefed.sh:360-368` validates the base SHA and reads `compare/<base_sha>...<expected_head>`, then validates its files. It no longer uses the mutable PR-files endpoint for this exception, so an A→B→A change cannot substitute another commit's scope.

Current verification: `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-pulse-merge-worker-briefed.sh` passes 75/75; ShellCheck passes. The existing trust-parity test contains the pinned-out-of-scope/live-in-scope regression added in the fix; today's broader parity rerun stopped at its earlier workflow-bot comment assertion before reaching services-sync cases (no code changes made in this retry).

<!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM67sQJf -->

@coderabbitai Verified addressed by existing commit bd82f4e009, already present on the PR head. `.agents/scripts/_worktree_dependency_snapshot.py:125-149` recursively checks required pnpm dependency links, excluding `optionalDependencies`; line 171 invokes it for each required importer entry point.

Verification: `python3 .agents/scripts/tests/test-worktree-dependency-provision.py` passed (41 tests, one filesystem-CoW skip). An isolated fixture check also confirmed rejection when required `bar` and its link are absent, acceptance when `bar` is optional or installed, and recursive rejection when installed `bar` requires absent `baz`. No further code change was necessary.

